  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It follows the same format as the earlier entries and leaves out ACME-421:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on HTTP 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nThe version and date come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files. ACME-421 was the only breaking change in the list (its title is marked with `!`, and it removed the `--legacy` flag). With it reverted, nothing in this release breaks existing usage, so a minor version bump to 2.4.0 fits. I didn't credit authors because the earlier entries don't.",
